From 54143cc4fb9c75ca507f9b744095e707e045a3c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:55:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(checks): stop four advisories from firing on correct
 books
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each of these was a false positive found on a real title. A checker that
flags good work teaches authors to ignore the whole report, so precision
here matters more than coverage.

  LANG-022  Skipped inside 《…》 and 〈…〉. Work titles are proper nouns:
            a sequel called 《明天不是默認值》 must survive a localisation
            pass intact, however mainland the wording reads.

  LANG-022  Dropped 「數據」 from the divergence table. Unlike 軟件/網絡 it
            is standard in Taiwan too, sitting beside 「資料」 with a
            narrower, numeric sense.

  A11Y-021  Only fires when the book declares a print source. A page-list
            maps to the pagination of a print edition; a digital-only book
            has nothing to map to.

  STORE-021 Skips the nav document. The span-per-character ratio measures
            inline cruft in prose, but a table of contents is mostly
            markup by nature — one class-driven span per entry trips the
            threshold no matter how cleanly it is written.

  ASSET-037 Goes quiet once a font licence file ships with the book, like
            every other check here, instead of repeating a reminder that
            has been acted on. Open licences (SIL OFL above all) require
            the licence text to travel with the font, so bundling it is
            both the compliance step and the evidence. --prune now keeps
            those files: no content document links to them, which is
            exactly the shape the orphan rule deletes.

Also removes a dead re.finditer loop in the store checks.

Adds TestAdvisoryPrecision, covering each case in both directions — the
false positive stays silent, the genuine defect still reports.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TWVhEKkpMiaADSLp97Qco3
